         IDENT     TOGETHER
* Results that are due in the same clock period: each arrives by its own way,
* and an instruction that issues in that clock takes it as an operand.
*
* The floating product of 064 is due 7 clock periods after it issues, the sum
* of 060 after 3, the shift of 054 after 2 and the logical product of 044
* after 1.  Issued 4, 5 and 6 clock periods behind the product they are all
* due with it, and the instructions behind them read all four.  The address
* registers do the same with the product of 032 (4), the sum of 030 (2) and a
* constant (1), and with the two counts of 026 and 027.  Every result is
* stored, for the comparison with the reference model.
*
* Direct start: exchange package at words 0-17 (monitor mode), code at word 40.
TEXIT    =         O'17777762           test exit register
OUT      =         O'2000
         ORG       0
         CON       P.START*O'100000000                 word 0: P (bits 47:24), A0
         CON       0                                   word 1: IBA, A1
         CON       O'7777774100000000                  word 2: ILA max, monitor mode
         CON       O'0000000030000000000000            word 3: XA = 1, VL = 64
         CON       0                                   word 4: DBA, cluster 0
         CON       O'7777774000000000                  word 5: DLA max
         BSSZ      D'10
         ORG       O'40
START    S4        K2,0
         S5        K3,0
         S3        O'1234567
         A3        7
         A5        O'11
* 064 at 1, due at 8; three PASS; 060 at 5, 054 at 6, 044 at 7: all due at 8
         S1        S4*FS5
         PASS
         PASS
         PASS
         S2        S4+S5
         S3        S3<10
         S6        S4&S5
         S7        S1!S2               two of them in the clock they arrive
         S0        S3\S6               and the other two
         OUT,0     S7
         OUT+1,0   S0
         OUT+2,0   S1
         OUT+3,0   S2
         OUT+4,0   S3
         OUT+5,0   S6
* once more over registers that hold something else, read a clock later
         S1        S6
         S2        S6
         S1        S4*FS5
         PASS
         PASS
         PASS
         S2        S5-S4
         S3        S3>3
         S6        #S4&S5
         PASS
         S7        S1\S2
         S0        S3!S6
         OUT+6,0   S7
         OUT+7,0   S0
* the A registers: 032 at 1, due at 5; a PASS; 030 at 3, 022 at 4: all due at 5
         A1        A3*A5
         PASS
         A2        A3+A5
         A4        O'31
         A7        A1+A2               the product and the sum in the clock they arrive
         A0        A4+A1               and the constant
         OUT+10,0  A7
         OUT+11,0  A0
         OUT+12,0  A1
         OUT+13,0  A2
         OUT+14,0  A4
* the population count (4) and the leading zero count (3) with a sum (2)
         S1        O'7070707
         A1        PS1
         A2        ZS1
         A4        A3+A5
         A7        A1+A2
         A0        A4+A7
         OUT+15,0  A7
         OUT+16,0  A0
         A6        0
         TEXIT,0   A6
HANG     J         HANG
K2       CON       O'0400014000000000000000             2.0
K3       CON       O'0400026000000000000000             3.0
         END
